Packaged-launcher follow-up
---------------------------
Attempt 1: 75-second bound. The packaged executable resolved TitleLogo,
PressStart, and SysPALInfo and emitted all seven title effects just as Xvfb's
bound expired, before input injection. Not counted as a pass.

Attempt 2: self-cleaning 120-second driver, stopped at 130 seconds while disc
resources were still initializing. At that point the process was using about
99% CPU while two pre-existing debugger loops were also each using about 100%
CPU. All attempt processes were removed. Not counted as a pass.

The packaged executable is byte-identical to the directly verified release
binary. The launcher attempts remain explicitly inconclusive under concurrent
host CPU pressure rather than being reported green.

